# Hardware Configuration

## Pin Assignments
### Button Matrix
- Column Pins: 10, 16, 14, 15, A0, A1, 8, 9
- Row Pins: 3, 4, 5, 6, 7

### Other Hardware
- LED Data Pin: 2 (WS2812B strip)
- Potentiometer 1: A2
- Potentiometer 2: A3

## Matrix Layout
The button matrix is physically arranged as two 5x4 matrices side by side, creating an 8x5 matrix:
```
[0,1,2,3,4]     [Row 1]
[5,6,7,8,9]     [Row 2]
[10,11,12,13,14] [Row 3]
[15,16,17,18,19] [Row 4]
[39,38,37,36,35] [Row 5]
[34,33,32,31,30] [Row 6]
[29,28,27,26,25] [Row 7]
[24,23,22,21,20] [Row 8]
```

## LED Mapping
The WS2812B LED strip is wired in a serpentine pattern. The mapping between logical button positions and physical LED positions is defined in [firmware.ino](mdc:hardware/firmware/firmware.ino).

## Configuration Constants
- Debounce Delay: 10ms
- LED Blink Interval: 500ms
- Potentiometer Deadzone: 5 units
- Default Inactive Brightness: 25
- Default Active Brightness: 40
- Pressed Brightness: 255 (fixed)

## Communication
- Serial Baud Rate: 115200
- Protocol: 8N1 (8 data bits, no parity, 1 stop bit)
